  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ITP 295 Media Development in a Democratic Framework Georgia - ITP 259 Media Development in a Democratic Framework Georgia</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">ITP 295 Sj&#xe4;lvreglerande ramverk f&#xf6;r demokratisk mediautveckling Georgien</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">1) Individuals and organisations participating in the programme benefit from and leverage networks in terms of media regulatory and self-regulatory frameworks. These networks include national contacts in Georgia, collaborations with key actors in Sweden (as an EU Member State) and cooperation with relevant European institutions. 

2) Increased knowledge and capacity to initiate and implement structured, long-term transformation work within the participants&apos; respective organizations. 

3) That the participants, individually and together as a team, through a collaborative process in which key actors generate and develop ideas and actions adapted to the recommendations put forward by the European Commission on Georgia&apos;s candidacy for membership of the European Union.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">International Training Programme (ITP): &quot;Self-regulating frameworks for democratic media development&quot;. The programme aims at strengthening the capacity of strategically important actors and organisations in Georgia in their work to establish, support and protect self-regulating frameworks for media in support of freedom of speech.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Internationellt kapacitetsutvecklingsprogram (ITP) som syftar till att st&#xe4;rka strategiskt viktiga akt&#xf6;rer och organisationer i Georgien i deras arbete att etablera, st&#xf6;tta och skydda institutioner som ing&#xe5;r i yttrandefrihetens sj&#xe4;lvreglerande ramverk, genom att aktivt till&#xe4;mpa den teoretiska och praktiska kunskap som erh&#xe5;llits genom programmet. Genomf&#xf6;rare &#xe4;r NIRAS Sweden AB, ledningsansvarig part, i konsortium med International Media Support (IMS), Linn&#xe9;universitetet (FOJO: Medieinstitutet) och Global Reporting Sweden AB, som har tilldelats ramavtalet efter upphandling.</narrative>
  </description>
